WEBVTT

00:28.190 --> 00:30.500
<i>If we win this, we'll go to nationals!</i>

00:30.500 --> 00:32.200
ICHINAN HIGH SCHOOL - 2ND YEAR
ISAGI YOICHI

00:32.200 --> 00:35.700
REGIONAL HIGH SCHOOL SOCCER TOURNAMENT
SAITAMA PREFECTURE FINALS

00:34.070 --> 00:35.610
ICHINAN VS MATSUKAZE KOKUOU

00:35.700 --> 00:37.530
ICHINAN, MATSUKAZE KOKUOU

00:37.620 --> 00:38.740
Push up, Isagi!

00:38.830 --> 00:41.200
This is our last chance!
We believe in you!

00:41.290 --> 00:44.710
<i>Nationals!</i>

00:44.790 --> 00:46.420
<i>I'm here, loser!</i>

00:47.920 --> 00:49.800
<i>I could shoot.</i>

00:51.630 --> 00:53.170
<i>Nationals!</i>

00:54.300 --> 00:55.590
Isagi!

00:55.680 --> 00:56.970
Over here! I'm open!

00:57.550 --> 00:58.390
<i>Tada-chan?</i>

00:59.100 --> 01:01.310
<i>If I pass, we can score a goal.</i>

01:01.390 --> 01:02.770
Isagi!

01:02.850 --> 01:05.230
Don't forget!
One for all, all for one!

01:05.310 --> 01:10.480
<i>Right.
Soccer is an 11-player team sport.</i>

01:12.940 --> 01:15.110
<i>Alright! Now he can score.</i>

01:16.280 --> 01:17.160
<i>Seriously?</i>

01:18.450 --> 01:19.330
Attack!

01:19.410 --> 01:20.740
Press!

01:26.370 --> 01:28.560
MATSUKAZE KOKUOU HIGH SCHOOL - 2ND YEAR
KIRA RYOSUKE

01:28.630 --> 01:29.630
<i>The situation is dire!</i>

01:29.710 --> 01:32.510
-Stop him!
-Get past them all!

01:37.640 --> 01:40.550
ICHINAN, MATSUKAZE KOKUOU

01:46.140 --> 01:47.940
Sorry, guys!

01:48.850 --> 01:49.860
If I,

01:50.360 --> 01:51.820
could have scored.

01:52.730 --> 01:55.070
It's not your fault, Tada-chan .

01:56.110 --> 01:57.200
Forgive me!

01:58.780 --> 01:59.950
Kira-kun!

02:00.030 --> 02:01.120
So cool!

02:01.200 --> 02:04.580
Kira, people call you
the treasure of Japanese soccer.

02:04.660 --> 02:08.580
You've even been invited
to play for the Japan U-18 team.

02:08.670 --> 02:10.630
-What are your thoughts?
-Let's see.

02:11.170 --> 02:14.550
For now, my goal is to win nationals with my team.

02:15.220 --> 02:16.830
I can only say this,

02:17.300 --> 02:22.100
the reason I'm here is my teammates.

02:22.180 --> 02:24.220
Kira, you're awesome!

02:25.270 --> 02:26.930
You did well.

02:27.020 --> 02:28.690
The third-years are leaving.

02:29.230 --> 02:32.650
Be proud of these days you spent together as a team.

02:32.730 --> 02:36.570
One day, this defeat in your lives,

02:41.030 --> 02:45.830
don't forget that it wasn't meaningless!

02:46.410 --> 02:53.090
For me, the Ichinan Team is Japan's best soccer team!

02:53.170 --> 02:54.040
<i>No.</i>

02:55.170 --> 02:57.010
<i>We couldn't reach nationals.</i>

02:57.630 --> 02:59.760
<i>Because we were eliminated in the regionals.</i>

03:05.010 --> 03:08.980
<i>And on this team, I'm an unknown second-year forward.</i>

03:09.690 --> 03:10.900
<i>These are the facts.</i>

03:12.480 --> 03:14.570
<i>Sorry, Noa-sama.</i>

03:16.400 --> 03:18.280
<i>A star player like you,</i>

03:18.360 --> 03:20.670
EUROPE'S BEST - FRANCE NATIONAL TEAM
NOEL NOA

03:24.870 --> 03:26.490
<i>What a volley!</i>

03:26.580 --> 03:29.870
<i>What a goal!</i>

03:29.960 --> 03:32.290
<i>I don't think I can become like that.</i>

03:32.370 --> 03:33.670
You're amazing, Yo-chan!

03:33.750 --> 03:35.040
You're unstoppable!

03:35.130 --> 03:36.750
<i>I admired you.</i>

03:36.840 --> 03:38.050
Nice shot!

03:38.130 --> 03:40.260
You're definitely not middle school level!

03:40.340 --> 03:44.010
<i>I kept playing soccer, but…</i>

03:44.090 --> 03:46.760
One for all, all for one!

03:46.850 --> 03:48.520
Let's go to nationals together!

03:48.600 --> 03:49.640
-Okay!
-Okay!

03:49.730 --> 03:52.850
<i>Apparently my dreams will remain just dreams.</i>

03:53.480 --> 03:56.610
<i>One day, I dreamed of becoming a star player for the Japan National Team</i>

03:57.690 --> 04:03.860
<i>and having a foolish dream like winning the World Cup.</i>

04:10.040 --> 04:14.670
<i>If instead of passing there</i>

04:17.460 --> 04:18.880
<i>I had taken a shot</i>

04:22.380 --> 04:25.590
<i>would my destiny have changed?</i>

04:30.350 --> 04:35.440
One for all.
All for one.

04:36.860 --> 04:40.440
Soccer is a game played with 11 people.

04:40.940 --> 04:42.490
You can't do it alone.

04:52.040 --> 04:53.910
Damn it.

04:54.540 --> 04:56.920
I wanted to win.

04:59.040 --> 05:00.340
<i>I'm back.</i>

05:01.340 --> 05:04.260
Welcome back, how was the match?

05:04.340 --> 05:07.090
We lost. I'm hungry.

05:07.180 --> 05:10.060
Too bad. I made pork chops special for today.

05:10.140 --> 05:13.980
That kind of thing is normally eaten before a match.

05:14.060 --> 05:15.020
Oh, is that so?

05:15.100 --> 05:17.100
It's delicious, just eat it.

05:17.600 --> 05:23.490
By the way, you got a letter.
From a place called the Japan Football Union.

05:26.450 --> 05:28.410
'Certified Athlete'?

05:28.490 --> 05:31.160
That means something good, right?

05:31.240 --> 05:32.580
I don't know!

05:34.080 --> 05:36.540
<i>Why me?</i>

05:42.920 --> 05:45.550
<i>Are we sure this is the place?</i>

05:45.630 --> 05:47.720
You're from the Ichinan team,

05:47.800 --> 05:49.680
you're Isagi-kun, right?

05:50.300 --> 05:53.770
So they called you too. Thanks for the other day.

05:53.850 --> 05:55.520
Do you remember me?

05:55.600 --> 05:58.060
Kira-kun.

05:58.150 --> 06:01.480
Of course. We just lost to you guys the other day, after all.

06:01.570 --> 06:04.610
I remember you very well.

06:04.690 --> 06:06.900
Your field of vision is very wide,

06:06.990 --> 06:08.740
and your soccer IQ is high.

06:08.820 --> 06:12.490
I was thinking if we were on the same team, you'd give me great passes.

06:12.580 --> 06:14.200
Thank you very much.

06:14.290 --> 06:17.960
<i>Seriously? Kira Ryosuke is praising me?</i>

06:18.040 --> 06:19.330
Shall we go then?

06:19.920 --> 06:22.710
Although I have no idea what we're going to do here.

06:22.800 --> 06:23.670
Really.

06:24.710 --> 06:28.050
No need for formalities. We're the same age, after all.

06:28.130 --> 06:29.640
Let's get along, Isagi-kun.

06:30.550 --> 06:31.550
Okay!

06:31.640 --> 06:33.680
<i>He's a really nice guy.</i>

06:35.270 --> 06:36.810
It looks like it's here.

06:45.900 --> 06:47.190
So crowded.

06:47.280 --> 06:49.700
I see some familiar faces too.

06:49.780 --> 06:51.910
Sennou's star, Okawa.

06:51.990 --> 06:54.700
The tallest high schooler, Ishikari.

06:55.410 --> 06:58.040
Aomori's Messi Nishioka is here too.

06:58.120 --> 07:01.790
<i>Is it just me or is everyone here a forward?</i>

07:06.710 --> 07:09.970
Congratulations, rough diamonds.

07:10.800 --> 07:13.970
You are the 300 forwards under 18 I selected

07:14.050 --> 07:17.310
with my arbitrary judgment and biases.

07:17.390 --> 07:19.520
I am Ego Jinpachi,

07:19.600 --> 07:24.480
the man who will make Japan win the World Cup.

07:26.780 --> 07:29.400
<i>What did he just say?</i>

07:29.490 --> 07:32.410
<i>'Win the World Cup?'</i>

07:33.660 --> 07:34.990
Who's that?

07:35.080 --> 07:35.990
Do you know him?

07:36.080 --> 07:37.580
No, not at all.

07:37.660 --> 07:39.160
Simply put,

07:39.250 --> 07:44.170
for Japanese soccer to become the best in the world, it needs just one thing.

07:44.250 --> 07:47.250
The birth of a revolutionary forward.

07:47.340 --> 07:49.630
I will manage the experiment that will make the best forward in the world

07:49.720 --> 07:53.050
from among these 300.

07:53.550 --> 07:55.430
That's the purpose of this facility.

07:56.260 --> 07:57.470
Blue Lock.

07:58.520 --> 08:01.480
<i>From today, you will live here</i>

08:01.560 --> 08:05.270
<i>and undergo my specially designed training.</i>

08:05.360 --> 08:07.070
<i>You cannot return home</i>

08:07.150 --> 08:10.670
<i>and you'll leave behind everything about soccer up to now.</i>

08:10.690 --> 08:12.360
But I promise you this.

08:12.450 --> 08:16.700
The last one standing after defeating the other 299 people here

08:16.780 --> 08:21.290
will become the world's best forward.

08:21.370 --> 08:24.290
That's all, good luck.

08:28.250 --> 08:30.710
<i>What is he talking about?</i>

08:31.220 --> 08:33.220
Excuse me, can I have your attention?

08:33.800 --> 08:36.050
I can't accept these conditions.

08:36.140 --> 08:38.930
We all have teams we care about.

08:39.010 --> 08:41.640
Some of us are even going to nationals.

08:41.730 --> 08:46.730
I can't leave my team and join some shady program like this.

08:46.810 --> 08:49.150
He's right. I'm also going to nationals.

08:49.230 --> 08:52.070
And where did this suddenly living here come from?

08:52.150 --> 08:53.450
And who are you anyway?

08:53.530 --> 08:55.500
Bring someone proper to explain.

08:58.450 --> 09:02.080
I see. So you're all sick.

09:03.370 --> 09:04.410
Unlock it.

09:04.500 --> 09:06.630
Those who want to leave can leave.

09:08.130 --> 09:11.090
Rather than becoming the world's best forward,

09:11.170 --> 09:15.800
is being the best on a high school team in this backward country more important?

09:17.140 --> 09:21.220
Even the thought of entrusting Japan's future to you makes me sick.

09:21.310 --> 09:22.890
<i>Huh?</i>

09:22.980 --> 09:24.100
Listen.

09:24.690 --> 09:27.900
The Japan Football Organization's strength is top-class.

09:27.980 --> 09:31.320
You could attribute that to the thoughtfulness of the Japanese.

09:31.400 --> 09:34.530
But everything else is second-rate.

09:35.110 --> 09:38.120
What is soccer to you?

09:38.200 --> 09:41.330
The combined strength of 11 people?

09:41.410 --> 09:43.040
Valuing bonds?

09:43.120 --> 09:44.540
Sacrifice?

09:44.620 --> 09:46.080
Teammates?

09:46.670 --> 09:50.670
That's why the country's soccer is always weak.

09:51.880 --> 09:53.260
<i>Let me tell you the answer.</i>

09:53.340 --> 09:59.390
Soccer is a sport where you score more goals than your opponent.

09:59.470 --> 10:02.600
The one who scores the most goals is the best.

10:02.680 --> 10:05.850
For those who want to play friendship, the door is there.

10:07.270 --> 10:10.610
<i>What is this guy talking about? This is nonsense.</i>

10:11.650 --> 10:14.280
What you're saying is terrible.
Please take back your words.

10:14.360 --> 10:18.530
There are tons of athletes in Japan to be respected.

10:18.610 --> 10:22.870
We grew up watching their 11-player struggles.

10:22.950 --> 10:25.200
They are my stars!

10:25.290 --> 10:27.460
You are wrong!

10:29.420 --> 10:31.920
Hm? The Japan National Team?

10:34.760 --> 10:38.470
Have they ever won the World Cup before?

10:38.550 --> 10:41.390
We're talking about becoming the best in the world here.

10:43.640 --> 10:46.270
<i>'Instead of supporting your team and winning 1-0,</i>

10:46.350 --> 10:50.850
<i>it's better to score a hat trick and lose 3-4.'</i>

10:51.810 --> 10:56.650
These are the words of Noel Noa, who beat Messi and Cristiano Ronaldo to win the Ballon d'Or,

10:56.740 --> 11:00.700
the current best forward in the world.

11:01.320 --> 11:05.040
<i>Eric Cantona, 'To hell with my team.'</i>

11:05.120 --> 11:06.660
<i>'As long as I stand out.'</i>

11:07.200 --> 11:12.920
<i>Pelé, 'The world's best forward, midfielder, defender, and goalkeeper.'</i>

11:13.000 --> 11:16.250
<i>'No matter who you ask, the answer for all of them is me.'</i>

11:17.760 --> 11:19.970
What do you say to that? Isn't it terrible?

11:20.050 --> 11:22.300
But all these guys are the best!

11:22.390 --> 11:25.970
And they are all extraordinary egoists!

11:26.060 --> 11:29.480
That's what Japanese soccer lacks.

11:30.390 --> 11:35.690
If you can't be the number one egoist, you can't be the number one forward.

11:38.030 --> 11:39.650
<i>I'm sure what this man is saying</i>

11:39.740 --> 11:43.950
I want to produce such a person in this country.

11:44.660 --> 11:46.540
<i>is wrong.</i>

11:47.910 --> 11:51.540
<i>The one who will stand atop 299 corpses</i>

11:52.290 --> 11:54.840
<i>is just a single hero.</i>

11:56.880 --> 12:00.260
<i>Impossible. I haven't even achieved anything yet.</i>

12:00.340 --> 12:03.590
Think about it. You're in the World Cup finals.

12:03.680 --> 12:07.600
<i>Eighty thousand people are watching and they're all focused on you.</i>

12:07.680 --> 12:09.270
<i>Score is 0-0.</i>

12:09.350 --> 12:11.020
<i>Extra time in the second half.</i>

12:11.100 --> 12:12.230
<i>Final attack.</i>

12:12.310 --> 12:14.650
<i>You, receiving a pass from your team,</i>

12:14.730 --> 12:16.650
<i>face off against the goalkeeper.</i>

12:16.730 --> 12:18.820
<i>There's a teammate 6 meters to your right.</i>

12:18.900 --> 12:22.200
<i>If you pass, it's a guaranteed goal.</i>

12:22.280 --> 12:25.820
<i>At that moment, when everyone's hopes and the championship depend on you,</i>

12:26.910 --> 12:31.540
<i>the crazy egoists who can shoot without hesitation.</i>

12:33.500 --> 12:35.670
Let them advance.

12:38.710 --> 12:40.710
Set aside your feelings.

12:40.800 --> 12:43.260
Here, you are the star.

12:46.050 --> 12:49.180
<i>No one taught me these things.</i>

12:49.260 --> 12:52.020
Nothing can make you happier than reaching your goals.

12:52.100 --> 12:54.640
Live only for that moment.

12:57.060 --> 12:59.860
That's what a forward is, right?

13:04.030 --> 13:06.780
<i>I am a forward!</i>

13:08.990 --> 13:10.490
Isagi-kun?

13:10.580 --> 13:12.450
I'll do it too, you bastard!

13:12.950 --> 13:13.830
Me too!

13:27.590 --> 13:29.050
<i>Shall we begin?</i>

13:31.060 --> 13:37.600
<i>The place where soccer is most intense in the world, Blue Lock.</i>

13:48.950 --> 13:52.660
Since my number is 299Z, it must be room Z.

13:53.200 --> 13:55.080
Oh, I found it.

14:05.590 --> 14:06.930
Isagi-kun.

14:07.010 --> 14:10.180
Thank goodness. There's someone I know in the room.

14:10.260 --> 14:11.720
Kira-kun.

14:12.640 --> 14:13.810
I'm relieved too.

14:14.720 --> 14:15.600
Oh, sorry.

14:17.140 --> 14:18.520
I threw it too hard.

14:19.310 --> 14:21.860
No, no, it's okay.

14:21.940 --> 14:23.900
-Watch where you step.
-What?

14:26.900 --> 14:29.240
Hey, Zico. Pass.

14:29.320 --> 14:31.320
Pass the ball, Zico.

14:31.910 --> 14:33.790
<i>What kind of dream is he having?</i>

14:36.750 --> 14:39.330
Are you that Kira Ryosuke?

14:39.420 --> 14:41.250
Wow, it really is him.

14:41.330 --> 14:42.960
Oh, thanks.

14:43.880 --> 14:45.300
Nice to meet you.

14:45.380 --> 14:47.920
My name is Igarashi Gurimu.

14:48.010 --> 14:49.630
Nice to meet you too.

14:49.720 --> 14:51.800
My family lives at a temple.

14:51.890 --> 14:54.140
But I never want to be there.

14:54.220 --> 14:56.980
I got excited when I heard what that guy said earlier.

14:57.060 --> 15:00.190
I thought, 'The opportunity to change my life has come to me.'

15:01.150 --> 15:04.650
<i>Have you changed your clothes, rough diamonds?</i>

15:06.190 --> 15:07.690
<i>Hello, hello.</i>

15:07.780 --> 15:11.200
<i>The people you're in the same room with right now are both your roommates</i>

15:11.280 --> 15:13.370
<i>and your rivals who will help you improve.</i>

15:13.990 --> 15:16.620
<i>Your abilities,</i>

15:16.700 --> 15:19.500
<i>have been ranked according to my arbitrary judgment.</i>

15:19.580 --> 15:21.880
<i>That's what the numbers on your jerseys mean.</i>

15:22.460 --> 15:26.210
<i>So you can see where you rank among the 300.</i>

15:26.300 --> 15:30.680
<i>299? That's awful, I'm extremely weak.</i>

15:30.760 --> 15:35.510
<i>That number will change based on training and matches.</i>

15:35.600 --> 15:39.060
<i>As a result, the top 5 players will unconditionally</i>

15:39.140 --> 15:41.390
<i>enter the tournament to be held in 6 months,</i>

15:41.480 --> 15:45.900
<i>where forwards for the U-20 World Cup will be selected.</i>

15:46.400 --> 15:50.070
<i>U-20, as in the Japan National Team?</i>

15:50.150 --> 15:55.280
<i>Also, those eliminated from Blue Lock from now on</i>

15:57.340 --> 16:01.260
<i>will never be able to play on the Japan National Team.</i>

16:04.290 --> 16:07.590
<i>What you need to win here is ego.</i>

16:07.670 --> 16:10.300
<i>Now we'll do a test to measure it.</i>

16:10.380 --> 16:13.510
<i>Alright, game time.</i>

16:13.590 --> 16:16.390
<i>You have 136 seconds.</i>

16:16.470 --> 16:18.520
<i>The person touched by the ball becomes 'it'.</i>

16:18.600 --> 16:22.560
<i>At the end of the time, the one who is 'it' is eliminated.</i>

16:22.640 --> 16:23.980
<i>What did you say?</i>

16:24.060 --> 16:26.560
<i>Oh, and also, using hands is prohibited.</i>

16:30.440 --> 16:32.820
This isn't soccer.

16:32.900 --> 16:35.780
So because I'm the weakest, I'm the first 'it'?

16:36.700 --> 16:38.410
Let's do it then.

16:38.490 --> 16:40.040
No hard feelings, okay?

16:40.120 --> 16:43.540
Hey, wait. Do you really believe what he said?

16:43.620 --> 16:45.380
But if it's true, what will I do?

16:47.420 --> 16:48.750
I'll do it.

16:48.840 --> 16:51.340
If I lose, I'll become a temple monk.

16:52.920 --> 16:57.140
<i>Whoever is eliminated from here can never play for the Japan National Team again.</i>

17:02.520 --> 17:04.020
Hey, don't come here!

17:04.100 --> 17:05.520
Sorry, Isagi!

17:05.600 --> 17:07.400
-What?
-Amen!

17:08.900 --> 17:10.190
Damn it!

17:10.780 --> 17:12.610
This is nothing but nonsense.

17:12.690 --> 17:16.160
I came here to prove him wrong.

17:16.950 --> 17:18.490
Are you kidding me!

17:18.580 --> 17:20.830
This is absolutely wrong.

17:20.910 --> 17:23.200
I won't let him ruin my future!

17:23.290 --> 17:26.500
Damn it, I can't hit anyone!

17:29.840 --> 17:32.920
This guy is still sleeping. Gotcha!

17:39.050 --> 17:41.850
Hey, that's a foul!

17:41.930 --> 17:43.980
If we were in a match, that'd definitely be a red card!

17:44.010 --> 17:46.640
The only thing forbidden is using your hands, right?

17:47.150 --> 17:48.560
Good morning.

17:48.650 --> 17:50.360
<i>Who is this guy?</i>

17:51.020 --> 17:54.150
Hey, I don't like playing dirty.

17:54.240 --> 17:56.200
Play fair.

17:56.280 --> 17:58.160
Mr. Serious, are you?

18:02.700 --> 18:04.830
You left an opening, amen.

18:06.790 --> 18:08.040
Jerk.

18:08.540 --> 18:10.210
I'll destroy you.

18:10.790 --> 18:12.090
-Over here!
-Hey!

18:12.670 --> 18:14.800
BL RANK - 291
KUNIGAMI RENSUKE

18:14.880 --> 18:16.050
Don't!

18:19.930 --> 18:21.390
-Amen.
-Isagi-kun?

18:21.470 --> 18:24.100
Ah, sorry. I wasn't aiming for you.

18:28.560 --> 18:29.480
<i>The situation is bad.</i>

18:30.060 --> 18:35.150
<i>If I can't hit anyone in one minute, my soccer career is over.</i>

18:36.030 --> 18:39.570
<i>It can't end in a place like this!</i>

18:41.280 --> 18:42.410
I'm saved!

18:42.490 --> 18:43.700
<i>They're too athletic.</i>

18:43.790 --> 18:46.410
<i>If I don't aim properly, I won't hit anyone.</i>

18:47.160 --> 18:49.830
<i>I should target someone weaker than me.</i>

18:50.420 --> 18:53.590
I won't let you catch me!

18:54.630 --> 18:57.720
<i>Wait, is my fate really going to be decided like this?</i>

19:01.260 --> 19:03.390
<i>Terrible, beyond terrible!</i>

19:03.470 --> 19:06.770
<i>No. I don't want to lose. I don't want it to end like this!</i>

19:07.270 --> 19:10.100
<i>I'll do anything. I want to win!</i>

19:10.190 --> 19:13.570
<i>I want to continue playing soccer!</i>

19:13.650 --> 19:16.320
<i>I don't want my dreams to end!</i>

19:17.780 --> 19:21.070
-You little! Get off me!
-Hit while you have the chance!

19:21.160 --> 19:22.530
Let me go!

19:22.620 --> 19:24.240
Go that way!

19:24.330 --> 19:27.620
I told you to play fair, didn't I?

19:31.120 --> 19:32.290
Get off me now!

19:34.960 --> 19:37.840
Shit, wait. Time out.

19:39.840 --> 19:41.220
Isagi-kun, hit him!

19:41.300 --> 19:42.430
While you have the chance!

19:45.220 --> 19:48.810
Hey, wait. Don't come. Stay away!

19:48.890 --> 19:51.520
I don't want it to end in a place like this!

19:52.480 --> 19:55.060
<i>I can win. I can survive.</i>

19:55.570 --> 19:59.400
-Please, don't!
<i>-But his soccer life would end.</i>

20:01.360 --> 20:05.370
<i>No, I have to. This is that kind of place.</i>

20:06.120 --> 20:09.330
<i>If there's a winner somewhere, there has to be a loser too.</i>

20:10.330 --> 20:15.750
<i>Realizing my own dream means taking someone else's dream away.</i>

20:30.310 --> 20:31.560
This is wrong.

20:35.100 --> 20:38.610
I can never change like this.

20:39.610 --> 20:41.650
<i>I came here to change my life.</i>

20:41.740 --> 20:44.410
<i>I came to become the best in the world!</i>

20:45.450 --> 20:49.620
<i>If I don't target someone stronger than me, I can't change anything.</i>

20:49.700 --> 20:50.910
I like you.

20:53.410 --> 20:54.250
Just as you said.

20:54.330 --> 20:55.290
If you're going to crush,

20:57.420 --> 20:59.550
BL Rank - 290
BACHIRA MEGURU

20:57.420 --> 20:59.550
crush the strongest!

21:03.720 --> 21:04.590
Me?

21:14.980 --> 21:16.480
<i>One day someone said:</i>

21:17.270 --> 21:19.690
<i>'In the world of soccer</i>

21:19.770 --> 21:24.860
<i>you can train a first-class goalkeeper, defense, and midfield</i>

21:24.950 --> 21:27.780
<i>but you can't train a forward.'</i>

21:29.410 --> 21:32.040
<i>'A first-class forward,</i>

21:32.750 --> 21:36.790
<i>at the place where soccer is most intense'</i>

21:36.870 --> 21:39.670
The strongest one…

21:39.750 --> 21:41.000
Boom!

21:49.010 --> 21:52.100
<i>'appears on its own.'</i>

23:29.900 --> 23:32.530
<i>A Blue Lock, Extra Time!</i>

23:33.620 --> 23:37.580
Your mother and I don't know much about soccer, but

23:38.200 --> 23:41.290
being selected by the JFA is a great thing, Yoichi.

23:41.370 --> 23:42.790
Isn't it?

23:42.880 --> 23:48.260
After all, you've been great at soccer since you were little.

23:51.380 --> 23:52.430
You could say that.

23:52.510 --> 23:58.140
Even for Christmas, you asked Santa for the World Cup,

23:58.220 --> 24:02.730
and your future goal was always to become the world's best forward.

24:02.810 --> 24:05.570
Could you stop now? It's so embarrassing.

24:05.650 --> 24:10.150
<i>Whenever there was a match on TV, you'd be glued to the screen.</i>

24:10.240 --> 24:13.160
<i>And when we changed the channel, you'd start crying.</i>

24:13.700 --> 24:15.620
I want to watch the news.

24:15.700 --> 24:18.290
No!

24:18.370 --> 24:19.370
<i>Yes, yes.</i>

24:19.870 --> 24:22.790
<i>You wouldn't stop crying until you fell asleep.</i>

24:22.870 --> 24:25.130
<i>And when you woke up, you'd forget everything.</i>

24:26.040 --> 24:29.670
<i>Besides, you always forgot to do your homework.</i>

24:30.210 --> 24:33.220
That's why your grades aren't good.

24:33.300 --> 24:37.310
You're really lucky to have been selected, Yoichi.

24:37.390 --> 24:38.310
Right?

24:38.390 --> 24:41.730
It feels like you were making fun of me at the end though.